    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "### Is your feature request related to a problem? Please describe.\n\nWe currently refrain from turning annotated global variables into `cdef` variables to prevent them from disappearing from the module dict. However, their type information would be quite valuable given the many optimisations that we now apply to the builtin types.\n\n### Describe the solution you'd like.\n\nWe should make the type annotations of global variables available to type inference, so that their declared annotation type is used when reading the variable.\n\n### Describe alternatives you've considered.\n\nThere is a certain risk that type annotations might not reflect the value type found at runtime, but that seems a user side problem and nothing that Cython should care about. It might even uncover bugs if Cython starts reporting assignment errors at runtime.\n\nThere is also the risk that Cython starts rejecting subtypes of the declared builtin types, since it is more strict in requiring exact types for builtins. Time will tell whether that poses problems for users.\n\n### Additional context\n\n_No response_",
